# Secrets — MUST stay first, and this file MUST be committed before any other file is staged.
# Before this repository existed, `.env` was protected only because /home/anont/.gitignore line 2
# is `/*`, which ignored the entire tree. Creating a repository here removes that protection at the
# instant it is created, so this file is committed alone, first, as its own commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Evidence artifacts: large, and their integrity is already pinned by SHA-256 in DECISIONS.md and
# in the research documents. The irreplaceable material is the markdown record, not these blobs.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite.collector.lock
# Artifact backups: each is 3.7-4.4 GB and there are currently fourteen of them. They were
# untracked but NOT ignored, so a single `git add -A` would have tried to commit ~26 GB -- and
# this repository has already been bitten once by `git add -A` sweeping in files it should not.
*.bak
*.bak-wal
*.bak-shm

# Runtime state and caches
.autonomy/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# B11c watcher runtime state. Logs and receipts may reference collection artifacts and the
# supervisor state changes every poll; neither belongs in history.
research/b11a/supervisor_state.json
research/b11a/supervisor_state.json.tmp
research/b11a/supervisor.lock
research/b11a/watcher.pid
research/b11a/logs/
research/b11a/receipts/

# B15a shadow pilot runtime. Raw frames and the derived database are live mutable evidence, not
